## Scope — this licence covers the code in this repository, and only the code.

No dataset is vendored here. `data/` is git-ignored except
`data/external/*.manifest.json`, and each manifest carries its own dataset's
`licence` and `licence_url` fields. Those terms govern the data; this file does
not, and cannot, relicense them.

| Dataset | Licence | Vendored here? |
|---|---|---|
| Own synthetic merchant streams (`src/rakshak/generator/`) | MIT, as above — it is code in this repo | Output is generated, not committed |
| BAF — Bank Account Fraud (Feedzai, NeurIPS 2022) | **CC BY-NC-SA 4.0** (Kaggle dataset page) | **No.** Non-commercial + share-alike: usable inside git-ignored `data/`, not vendorable into an MIT repo |
| Online Retail II (UCI, ID 502) | CC BY 4.0 | No |

**The trap T-0015 recorded, stated here so nobody repeats it:** the Feedzai
`bank-account-fraud` **GitHub repository** ships an `LICENSE` that is
**Apache-2.0, and it covers their code, not their data.** The data is
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 under its Kaggle dataset page. Reading the GitHub `LICENSE` as
the data licence would be wrong in the direction that matters — it would make
an NC/SA dataset look vendorable into this MIT repo. It is not.

Nothing above conflicts with the MIT grant on this repository's code: MIT is
granted over files that are all original to this project, and no CC BY-NC-SA or
CC BY material is incorporated into them.
